1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,877
Part three: the Support section.

2
00:00:04,077 --> 00:00:09,716
Here you add two things: the patient's providers, and the patient's emergency contacts.

3
00:00:09,756 --> 00:00:12,214
Both come from PointClickCare.

4
00:00:14,114 --> 00:00:18,433
Both lists are on the patient's Profile tab in PointClickCare.

5
00:00:18,733 --> 00:00:23,308
Providers are under Medical Professionals. You add them one by one.

6
00:00:23,608 --> 00:00:27,564
Each one needs a full name, a phone number, and a specialty.

7
00:00:27,864 --> 00:00:34,913
Emergency contacts are under Contacts. You copy each one's name, phone number, and relationship.

8
00:00:35,213 --> 00:00:39,169
Then you paste them all into one answer box, as free text.

9
00:00:41,183 --> 00:00:44,456
In the assessment's menu on the left, click Support.

10
00:00:48,269 --> 00:00:52,993
The Support section opens. It starts with: Let's review Providers.

11
00:00:53,243 --> 00:00:58,287
You can choose Select from pre-defined list, Enter as free text, or N/A.

12
00:00:58,537 --> 00:01:05,863
Below it is the second question: Who is available in your support system to help you manage your health if needed?

13
00:01:06,113 --> 00:01:10,112
Start with the providers. You'll find them in PointClickCare.

14
00:01:11,436 --> 00:01:15,477
Switch to PointClickCare, where the patient's chart is open.

15
00:01:15,727 --> 00:01:17,647
Click the Profile tab.

16
00:01:20,769 --> 00:01:26,951
The Profile tab lists the patient's Contacts at the top, and Medical Professionals below.

17
00:01:28,269 --> 00:01:33,014
Scroll down to Medical Professionals. These are the patient's providers.

18
00:01:33,264 --> 00:01:37,860
Each row shows the first name, surname, profession, and office phone.

19
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:40,903
The primary physician is shown in bold.

20
00:01:42,336 --> 00:01:48,084
Start with the first provider: Ferdinand Akoko, a nurse practitioner, or NP.

21
00:01:48,336 --> 00:01:53,167
Copy the first name and surname together. That's the provider's full name.

22
00:01:53,417 --> 00:01:57,416
Then copy the profession, NP. It goes in Specialty.

23
00:01:57,669 --> 00:02:00,044
Then copy the office phone number.

24
00:02:02,869 --> 00:02:07,252
Tip: press the Windows key and V to open your clipboard history.

25
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:12,845
It keeps everything you copied, newest first: the phone number, NP, and the name.

26
00:02:13,095 --> 00:02:17,627
So copy all three first. Then paste each one where it belongs.

27
00:02:18,936 --> 00:02:22,572
Back in ThoroughCare, go to Let's review Providers.

28
00:02:24,390 --> 00:02:26,981
Choose Select from pre-defined list.

29
00:02:28,169 --> 00:02:35,816
A provider table appears. Enter all of the patient's providers here. If the patient has none, check Not Applicable.

30
00:02:36,066 --> 00:02:38,955
To add a provider, click New Provider.

31
00:02:41,569 --> 00:02:43,931
The New Provider window opens.

32
00:02:44,181 --> 00:02:51,209
It has fields for the provider's full name, phone number, fax number, specialty, address, and NPI.

33
00:02:51,459 --> 00:02:56,204
Click Provider Full Name, open the clipboard history, and paste the name.

34
00:02:57,702 --> 00:03:00,314
Paste the phone number into Phone Number.

35
00:03:00,702 --> 00:03:03,155
And paste NP into Specialty.

36
00:03:03,405 --> 00:03:05,057
Then click Save.

37
00:03:06,402 --> 00:03:11,361
The provider is added to the table, with the name, phone number, and specialty.

38
00:03:11,611 --> 00:03:16,378
Repeat these steps for every provider on the Medical Professionals list.

39
00:03:16,628 --> 00:03:21,011
The providers in ThoroughCare must match PointClickCare exactly.

40
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:28,196
Keep Select from pre-defined list chosen, and click New Provider for each one.

41
00:03:28,446 --> 00:03:31,707
To close the window without saving, click Back.

42
00:03:36,769 --> 00:03:43,008
Next question: Who is available in your support system to help you manage your health if needed?

43
00:03:43,258 --> 00:03:47,449
This means the patient's emergency contacts. Add them too.

44
00:03:47,702 --> 00:03:53,386
In PointClickCare, scroll up to Contacts, at the top of the same Profile tab.

45
00:03:53,636 --> 00:03:58,040
Copy the first contact's name, phone number, and relationship.

46
00:04:00,102 --> 00:04:04,229
In ThoroughCare, click in the answer box and paste the contact.

47
00:04:04,479 --> 00:04:09,736
Contacts go in as free text. You don't add them one by one, like providers.

48
00:04:10,002 --> 00:04:13,126
Copy the next contact from PointClickCare.

49
00:04:14,002 --> 00:04:17,487
Leave a blank line, and paste it below the first one.

50
00:04:17,737 --> 00:04:20,498
Repeat for every contact on the list.

51
00:04:25,636 --> 00:04:29,891
Each contact shows a name, a phone number, and a relationship.

52
00:04:30,141 --> 00:04:35,228
That completes Support: the provider list, and the emergency contacts list.

53
00:04:36,636 --> 00:04:38,160
Let's recap.

54
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:44,897
Open Support. In PointClickCare, open the Profile tab, and find Medical Professionals.

55
00:04:45,097 --> 00:04:51,506
Copy each provider's name, profession, and phone. Windows and V shows your clipboard history.

56
00:04:51,706 --> 00:04:57,390
Choose Select from pre-defined list, click New Provider, paste the details, and save.

57
00:04:57,590 --> 00:04:59,989
Repeat until both lists match.

58
00:05:00,189 --> 00:05:06,641
Then copy the patient's contacts, and paste them as free text, with a blank line between each one.

59
00:05:08,841 --> 00:05:11,681
That's part three. Support is done.

60
00:05:11,881 --> 00:05:16,157
In part four, you match the patient's allergies to PointClickCare.
